# DESCRIPTION

k1-usb2-phy drives the SpacemiT K1's USB 2 PHYs: the one at `0xc0a30000`, the UTMI PHY of the DWC3's high-speed port, which xhci(3) drives, and those at `0xc0940000` and `0xc09c0000`, the EHCI controllers', which ehci(3) drives and which only the vendor's tree describes (`ky,usb2-phy`).
devmgr(8) starts one for each by its record, after its clock's provider, and before the devices that link to it:

```text
driver k1-usb2-phy
class phy
match dt spacemit,k1-usb2-phy
match dt ky,usb2-phy
```

Its controller turns it on after releasing its own resets.
Turning it on turns its clock on through the clock's provider (k1-syscon(3): the APMU's USB 3 clock for the DWC3's, which the controller shares, and the EHCIs' own), waits up to 500 ms for its PLL to lock, then releases the PHY's internal reset, enables its clock gating, raises its high-speed transmitter's current a step, and sets its disconnect detector not to clear itself.
The registers and values are the vendor's.

# FILES

The tree is served in devmgr(8)'s, at `drivers/k1-usb2-phy-dt-<node>` (`phy@c0a30000`, `usbphy@c0940000`, `usbphy1@c09c0000`), and at `/dev/provider/<service>` in the drivers of the devices that link to it.

: `ctl`
  A command a line; it reads empty.
  `on` turns it on, again if it is on.
  Another line fails the write as invalid; so does `on` when the clock's provider refuses it or the PLL doesn't lock in 500 ms, and the driver logs which.
: `status`
  Read only.
  `PLL locked|unlocked`, as its register reads now; then `commands <n>, failed <n>`, and `last failure: on: <why>`.

